# S3 (second OWASP pass, GAP web-headers): security headers for the
# statically hosted PWA. Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_headers` format —
# these hosts pick this file up from the publish root and apply the
# headers to every response.
#
# NOTE: hosts that do not honor `_headers` (nginx, S3+CloudFront, a plain
# static server, …) MUST replicate these headers in their own config;
# the <meta http-equiv> CSP in index.html only covers the policy below,
# not the other headers.
#
# CSP rationale: the app loads only same-origin assets, calls the API on
# the same origin (/api/v1 — the Vite dev server proxies it, and any
# deployment should front it the same way), talks to Supabase over
# https/wss, and injects styles at runtime via Emotion (hence
# 'unsafe-inline' on style-src only). connect-src also allows a direct
# local API on :3000 for dev.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co http://localhost:3000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
